Rule 1 (size as integer must be non-negative to avoid negative dimension error)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≥ 0
>>
Rule 2 (size as tuple must have all non-negative dimensions to avoid negative dimension error)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= if v_1.len = 0 then true else ∀i ∈ [0, v_1.len - 1] : v_1[i] ≥ 0
>>
Rule 3 (size as integer bounded to prevent OOM)
{v_1 : int} |= v_1 ≤ 100000000
>>
Rule 4 (size as 1-D tuple bounded to prevent OOM)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 1 ∧ v_1[0] ≤ 100000000
>>
Rule 5 (size as 2-D tuple product bounded to prevent OOM)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 2 ∧ v_1[0] * v_1[1] ≤ 100000000
>>
Rule 6 (size as 3-D tuple product bounded to prevent OOM)
{v_1 : tuple(int)} |= v_1.len = 3 ∧ v_1[0] * v_1[1] * v_1[2] ≤ 100000000
